course: dictionary
lesson: 128
title: Adventure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An adventure is an exciting, unusual and sometimes risky experience or journey. Read the clues in this sentence: «Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves, and the fall is over: a lazy beginning that suddenly turns into a wild, dreamy adventure.» The words wild and suddenly turns tell you that the adventure is exciting and unexpected.
explain: Adventure can also mean the excitement of doing new and daring things, as in a love of adventure. The adjective is adventurous. A person who likes trying new and daring things is adventurous.
explain: Adventures can be everyday things too. In «camps and holiday clubs full of games, stories and adventures», a camp can be an adventure. Adventures should be planned with adults, and a dangerous dare is not an adventure.
fact: An adventure is an exciting, unusual and sometimes risky experience or journey.
fact: Adventure can mean the excitement of doing new and daring things.
fact: An adventure story is a story full of exciting events, often with a hero, a journey, danger and a happy ending.
fact: «Adventurous» means willing to try new and daring things.
fact: Adventures should be planned with adults, and dangerous dares are not adventures.
exercise: «Then, thump! thump! she lands on a heap of sticks and dry leaves, and the fall is over: a lazy beginning that suddenly turns into a wild, dreamy adventure.» What is the adventure in this sentence? | *An exciting, unusual experience | A pile of dry leaves | A boring sleep in bed
exercise: Which word is the adjective for someone who loves new and daring things? | *Adventurous | Careful | Quiet | Adventures
exercise: Which of these is a safe adventure? | *A camp planned with adults | Jumping off a roof for a bet | A dare to climb a dangerous cliff alone | Running onto a busy road
test: What does the phrase «go on an adventure» mean? | To go back home quietly | To stay still and wait | *To take part in an exciting, new experience
test: What is an adventure story? | *A story full of exciting events | A story with no characters | A maths problem
exam: Toad told Mole his «adventures» and «rather let himself go». What do adventures most likely mean here? | Things he owned | Hungry meals | Boring rules to follow | *Exciting experiences he had
